From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LIMInGZE666 <limingze666@users.noreply.gitcode.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Expose KSldApp::isInhibited for the consumer test

The test_package consumer verifies the inhibit/uninhibit counter round
trip black-box, which requires reading the effective inhibit state.
Upstream declares isInhibited() in the private section; move the
declaration into the public "For testing" block where the same kind of
test hooks (idleId/setIdleId/setGraceTime) already live. The definition
(ksldapp.cpp) and the internal call sites are unchanged.

---
 ksldapp.h | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ksldapp.h b/ksldapp.h
index bcc711c..7ae8194 100644
--- a/ksldapp.h
+++ b/ksldapp.h
@@ -211,6 +211,17 @@ public:
     {
         m_lockGrace = msec;
     }
+    /**
+     * For testing
+     * @internal
+     *
+     * Moved here from the private section: the test_package consumer
+     * verifies the inhibit/uninhibit counter round trip black-box,
+     * which requires reading the effective inhibit state. The upstream
+     * header already exposes the same kind of test hooks publicly
+     * (idleId/setIdleId/setGraceTime).
+     **/
+    bool isInhibited() const;
 
     /**
      * @brief Returns whether software rendering is forced.
@@ -344,8 +355,6 @@ private:
      */
     void lockProcessRequestedUnlock();
 
-    bool isInhibited() const;
-
     void updateIdleTimeout();
 
     /**
